      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "#EXCLUSIVE An illegal immigrant from El Salvador charged in two separate Houston homicides now has an ICE detainer lodged—DHS asking Texas not to release him. \n\nAccording to DHS, Jefferson Adonay Velasquez-Torres is charged in the August 2025 killing of 17-year-old Angel Garcia at a house party and the April 2026 shooting death of 27-year-old Noah Ramirez outside a Houston nightclub. He also faces charges of aggravated robbery and unlawfully carrying a weapon.\n\nICE has lodged a detainer with the Harris County Jail, requesting that officials notify the agency before any release.\n\nDHS says Velasquez-Torres illegally entered the U.S. through Texas as a minor in 2014 and was released into the country by the Obama administration.\n\nAssistant Secretary Lauren Bis said, “This criminal illegal alien has been charged with TWO counts of murder after two fatal shootings in Houston. He would not be in our country if it weren’t for the reckless open-border policies of the Obama Administration. ICE asked officials in Texas to not release this heinous murderer from jail without notifying ICE. Thankfully, Texas cooperates with us and together we will ensure this public safety threat will never be loose on our streets.”",
      "text_resolved": "#EXCLUSIVE An illegal immigrant from El Salvador charged in two separate Houston homicides now has an ICE detainer lodged—DHS asking Texas not to release him. \n\nAccording to DHS, Jefferson Adonay Velasquez-Torres is charged in the August 2025 killing of 17-year-old Angel Garcia at a house party and the April 2026 shooting death of 27-year-old Noah Ramirez outside a Houston nightclub. He also faces charges of aggravated robbery and unlawfully carrying a weapon.\n\nICE has lodged a detainer with the Harris County Jail, requesting that officials notify the agency before any release.\n\nDHS says Velasquez-Torres illegally entered the U.S. through Texas as a minor in 2014 and was released into the country by the Obama administration.\n\nAssistant Secretary Lauren Bis said, “This criminal illegal alien has been charged with TWO counts of murder after two fatal shootings in Houston. He would not be in our country if it weren’t for the reckless open-border policies of the Obama Administration. ICE asked officials in Texas to not release this heinous murderer from jail without notifying ICE. Thankfully, Texas cooperates with us and together we will ensure this public safety threat will never be loose on our streets.”",
